<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίδρομ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>running round,
			encircling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοιαὶ δὲ π. ἄντυγές εἰσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.728
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλῆμναι π. ἀμφοτέρωθεν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				726
			</span></i> ; of the rim of a shield, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				458
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				495
			</span></i> ; of a net, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				3.99
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλον π. αἰὲν ἑλίσσων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					236
				</span></i>
			 : c. dat., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃλς] νήσοισι περίδρομος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					60
				</span></i>
			: dub. sens. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.463.54
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>wandering, roaming</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκέτις φυγὰς
			π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				350
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					472
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνὴ π</span>. <i>gadabout</i>
			woman, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				581
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>that can be run round</i>: hence, <i>standing
				apart, detached</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολώνη . . π. ἔνθα καὶ ἔνθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.812
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλὴ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Carc.
					1
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>circular</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				718
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>surrounded</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίλη . . ὄρεσι
			π</span>., of Laconia, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1083
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. οὔρεσι γαῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.1085
				</span></i>
			.</div>
